# Native client, the second of two (sfcop --input): boot to the main menu, open Multiplayer, take
# the LAN (TCP/IP) path to the session browser, wait for the game multiplayer.steps hosts in the
# other client to be listed, select it and join, and reach the player list ("Multiplayer
# Startup") with both players shown. Needs a data folder with a stored key of its own: two
# clients never share one.
#
# Start the host first. The waits on screens are the marks multiplayer.steps names, which the
# build adds only when configured with
#
#   -DSFCOP_LIFT_EXTRA_MARKS=0x0046667A,0x00464D4F,0x00461C67,0x0046ED6A
#
# Coordinates are the game's display pixels (800x600, the 640x480 menu centred), as in
# menu.steps.

window 60 Starfleet Command

# --- the main menu, "Select Game"
waitmark 90 Select Game
sleep 1000

# --- MULTIPLAYER: Game Connections
click 563 348
waitmark 15 0x0046667A
sleep 2000

# --- LAN CONNECTIONS, TCP/IP: the session browser
click 487 322
waitmark 15 0x00464D4F

# --- the host announces its game about 50 s after its own start: wait for it, then UPDATE
# enumerates again and lists it
sleep 30000
click 279 506
sleep 5000

# --- the first row is the host's game; JOIN asks the host and opens the player list
click 175 174
sleep 1000
click 368 506
waitmark 30 0x0046ED6A

# --- both players in the list
sleep 20000
